Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals — Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers, BREF LVIC-AAF (@ic-aaf: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_45NWBJYAMXXSRV071A57EM02GB
European Commission, Joint Research Centre. Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals — Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers, BREF LVIC-AAF. 2007. [Official reference and full-text access](https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/reference/large-volume-inorganic-chemicals-ammonia-acids-and-fertilisers).

A substantial industrial reference for the ammonia, acid and fertiliser families, their linked feedstocks, process systems, resource requirements and residual streams.

Read the general material and the complete applicable production chapters, including process descriptions, quantities, emissions/consumptions, alternatives, integrated cases and supporting methods. Use the whole book for the sustained inorganic-process study; its technical descriptions need the independent thermodynamic, kinetic and material accounts developed here.

Identity, stated scope, date and official access were checked on 29 October 2026. This is a dated technical reference, not a claim that every described plant, technology or legal reference is current everywhere. Preserve its attribution, actual reuse notice and third-party exceptions; public access is not described as a blanket CC licence. Full-text or automated inspection limits are distinguished where relevant. No book, figure, industrial data or associated media is bundled.

